Package: rwidetable
Type: Package
Title: Disk-Backed Wide Tables with (Virtually) Unlimited Columns
Version: 1.4.1
Date: 2026-11-26
Authors@R: person("Nicolas", "Berta", email = "nicolas.berta@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides WIDETABLE, a reference class that stores each column of a
  table in its own file, so the number of columns is limited only by the storage
  space, while the table can be used much like a data.frame (subsetting, column
  extraction and replacement, row and column binding). Columns are loaded lazily
  into a size-limited in-memory cache. Also includes tools that convert parquet
  files and row chunks into per-column files that feed a WIDETABLE.
  This package was formerly named 'rbig'.
